      "supported": false,
      "issue": "The node claims 'Maintenance receiver M-A had boundary acceptance pending' based on a source (b678a...) that defines the term but does not provide evidence of M-A's specific status at shift start or during the event.",
      "evidenceNeeded": "A record showing M-A's role assignment and current authorization state relative to the work order release process at 09:48-10:00.","question":"What is the documented status (released/pending) of maintenance receiver M-A for WO-527 between shift start and the incident?"
    }, "node-1okpyu9": {
      "supported": false,
      "issue": "The node claims 'Alarm AL-44 display text... retained from earlier template' but cites a source (da026...) that only maps signal inputs to pressure conditions. It does not prove the specific label displayed or its history.",
      "evidenceNeeded": "A screenshot, log entry, or operator testimony confirming the exact alarm label shown on AL-44 at 10:00 and whether it differed from a standard 'LOW PRESSURE' message.","question":"What was the exact text string displayed by Alarm AL-44 when triggered?"
    }
  }, "decision": {
      "summary": "All three proposed nodes are currently unsupported because their supporting sources describe definitions or general logs but fail to provide direct evidence for the specific claims made (performed checks, M-A's status at that moment, actual alarm label). The investigation must request these missing records before accepting vulnerability factors.",
      "evidenceUsed": ["24ec1587-92e9-4320-82c2-30368d834f1d#1", "b678a928-a8d2-472d-bc03-2e1a3dc411e6#1", "da0260c0-7d49-43e8-b074-da2a14c7d59c#1"],
